Mac peers require Rex built-in Tailscale enabled in Rex Server settings and
one-time sign-in with the same Tailscale identity on each Mac. Keep access
restricted to the enrolling user. For outgoing HTTPS connections, connect the
standalone Tailscale app too: Rex embedded sharing does not provide macOS DNS/routes.
A .ts.net lookup failure usually means that client network prerequisite is missing.
Rex CLI tailscale-on is runtime-only; use the saved GUI setting for startup.
A sleeping, offline, or not-yet-enrolled peer stays pending without blocking Linux hosts.
The target Mac must be awake. No app/server restart or sleep-setting change is automatic.

Manual fallback: Settings (Cmd-comma), Remote Hosts, Add Remote Host.
Paste the full address, not the CLI label. Do not use ~ in place of HOME.

Native host backups: ~/.local/state/rex/client-host-backups/
Only the RexSync.servers preference is changed; unrelated preferences stay untouched.
Unreviewed app builds and host-directory formats fail without replacing the app or directory.
